b/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186159772 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e389798f-f44e-5b5b-afcd-2e7852474619" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186159773 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{5}{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186159773 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186159773 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "04531933-c48e-5b18-b0b0-c0907b8ac81a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186159774 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{10}{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186159774 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186159774 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "46a6904a-9a4b-5f70-b8cc-c0f4f9a23923" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186159775 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{7}{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186159775 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186159775 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6245a964-4af7-5b27-bc90-58eca4710df2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161689 #edb/ref 1069 "e-10298" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161689 #edb/ref 1071 "| $y$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $f_{Y|X}(y \\,|\\, 2)$ | $\\dfrac{2}{3}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{3}$ |\n\nFind the $\\textrm{E}\\big[Y \\,|\\, X=2\\big]$ given that the conditional probability mass function $f_{Y|X}(y \\,|\\, 2)$ is shown in the table above." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161689 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "07199b8b-32c6-59f5-b452-da48648cb799" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161689 #edb/ref 1074 "The conditional expected value of  $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\textrm{E}\\big[Y \\,|\\, X=x\\big] = \\sum_{y} y \\, f_{Y | X}(y \\,|\\, x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=2] & ={\\sum }_{y}y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,2) \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161692 #edb/ref 1069 "e-10305" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161692 #edb/ref 1071 "| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ | $\\dfrac{2}{9}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\dfrac{8}{27}$ | $\\dfrac{5}{27}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\dfrac{2}{27}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ |\n\nFind $\\textrm{E}\\big[Y \\,|\\, X=2\\big]$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161692 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2f074ddb-056a-51c6-b307-74df33f135f0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161692 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the conditional expected value of  $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\textrm{E}\\big[Y \\,|\\, X=x\\big] = \\sum_{y} y \\, f_{Y | X}(y \\,|\\, x).\n$$\n\nIn order to find $f_{Y | X}(y \\,|\\, x),$ let's first find the marginal distribution for $X,$ corresponding to the row totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | $f_X(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ | $\\dfrac{2}{9}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{3}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\dfrac{8}{27}$ | $\\dfrac{5}{27}$ | $\\dfrac{13}{27}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\dfrac{2}{27}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ | $\\dfrac{5}{27}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x$ is\n\n$$\nf_{Y | X}(y \\,|\\, x)  = \\dfrac{f(x,y)}{f_X(x)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding row total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x{:}$\n\n| $f_{Y | X}(y \\,|\\, x)$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\dfrac{1}{3}$ | $\\dfrac{2}{3}$ | $1$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\dfrac{8}{13}$ | $\\dfrac{5}{13}$ | $1$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\dfrac{2}{5}$ | $\\dfrac{3}{5}$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=2] & ={\\sum }_{y}y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,2) \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\frac{8}{13}+2\\cdot \\frac{5}{13} \\\\  & =\\frac{18}{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161699 #edb/ref 1069 "e-10350" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161699 #edb/ref 1071 "| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ | $\\dfrac{2}{9}$ |\n| $X=4$ | $\\dfrac{1}{3}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ |\n| $X=6$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ |\n\nFind $\\textrm{E}\\big[X \\,|\\, Y=1\\big]$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161699 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4de21bb7-7f18-56c4-9925-47459df6f049" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161699 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the conditional expected value of  $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\textrm{E}\\big[X \\,|\\, Y=y\\big] = \\sum_{x} x \\, f_{X | Y}(x \\,|\\, y).\n$$\n\nIn order to find $f_{X | Y}(x \\,|\\, y),$ let's first find the marginal distribution for $Y,$ corresponding to the column totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ | $\\dfrac{2}{9}$ |\n| $X=4$ | $\\dfrac{1}{3}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ |\n| $X=6$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ |\n| $f_Y(y)$ | $\\dfrac{5}{9}$ | $\\dfrac{4}{9}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y$ is\n\n$$\nf_{X | Y}(x \\,|\\, y)  = \\dfrac{f(x,y)}{f_Y(y)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding column total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y{:}$\n\n| $f_{X | Y}(x \\,|\\, y)$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $\\dfrac{1}{5}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ |\n| $X=4$ | $\\dfrac{3}{5}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ |\n| $X=6$ | $\\dfrac{1}{5}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ |\n|  | $1$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=1] & ={\\sum }_{x}x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,1) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}+4\\cdot \\frac{3}{5}+6\\cdot \\frac{1}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{5} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162123 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048317 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162123 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049149 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162123 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186162409 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162123 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186162410 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162123 #